 though, God, that is true.

104
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:03,980
 It's because, God, we want things to change

105
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:05,300
 because of Awaken.

106
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:10,560
 Change in our lives, change in our cities,

107
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:14,520
 and God, even across this country and our world, God.

108
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,440
 We believe it's possible, not because we're worthy.

109
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:21,760
 Lord, it is highly inappropriate for us to think

110
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:25,220
 that we're the ones through whom God might do it,

111
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:28,540
 which is why, God, we don't come and manufacture anything.

112
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:32,200
 It is inappropriate for us to pray

113
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,400
 that you would do revival through us,

114
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,320
 but God, it is appropriate for us to ask

115
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:41,460
 that you would do revival for us,

116
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:44,840
 for your heart is towards your people.

117
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:48,480
 And so God, come near to us now, we pray.

118
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,280
 In Christ's name, amen.

119
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,480
 - Man, it's good to see you guys.

120
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,640
 Okay, well, let me start off with this

121
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,840
 'cause we got a story that's gonna kick things off

122
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,400
 and hopefully set up our time together.

123
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:01,560
 When I met Brooke, who is my wife, in case you didn't know,

124
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,000
 it didn't take long before I knew

125
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,560
 that I wanted to date her.

126
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,960
 I was on the fence in the slightest

127
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:10,580
 because it was not hard to fall for a girl

128
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:13,680
 that loves beef fajitas over chicken fajitas.

129
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,300
 It wasn't hard to fall for a girl

130
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,120
 that doesn't take herself too seriously,

131
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,880
 is fine to be the butt of the joke.

132
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,080
 It wasn't hard to fall for a girl

133
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,160
 that was willing to poke fun at the guys,

134
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:25,520
 had never met a game that she did not want to play and win,

135
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,280
 and that came from a family that loved Jesus.

136
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:28,680
 I was in, the minute I met her, I was like,

137
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:32,480
 gosh, that girl's awesome, I want to date her.

138
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,860
 It was the easiest decision I made in college,

139
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:38,880
 but marrying Brooke, that was a much harder decision.

140
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:42,040
 Not because she did anything wrong.

141
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:43,880
 Quite the contrary.

142
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:48,880
 She did everything right, which I was not planning.

143
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:51,960
 She did all of it correct.

144
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:54,520
 It created for this massive problem in my life

145
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:56,880
 because I was the guy that was so low by choice.

146
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,440
 Some of you, you're in that spot.

147
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,440
 I preferred freedom over drama,

148
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,480
 and I knew as long as I was on my own, that was fine.

149
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,000
 Freedom is all that I was going to experience.

150
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,880
 I was a Bachelor to the Rapture sort of fella.

151
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,040
 That was my story.

152
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:10,400
 I was totally committed to living through college

153
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,400
 as a single.

154
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,960
 I didn't intend to find my girl while I was there.

155
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:16,160
 I wanted to find her out in the world.

156
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:16,980
 Why?

157
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:19,500
 Because I wanted to see her on the front lines of faith.

158
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,760
 I wanted to find my woman on the mission field.

159
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:25,560
 I wanted to find her chasing God and not some dude.

160
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:30,560
 And yet when Brooke entered my story and we began dating,

161
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:34,240
 I was the hypocrite because we were three years

162
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:37,920
 into the relationship and I realized something significant.

163
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:41,160
 I could not any longer live with one foot

164
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,760
 in a dating relationship with her

165
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:45,200
 and another foot trying to live the single lifestyle

166
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:47,120
 because fellas, just so you know,

167
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,540
 it is not a good husbandly rhythm to spend two hours

168
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:53,320
 at the gym or to order Chewy's combination fajita burritos

169
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:56,160
 or to get golfing on the weekends with the boys.

170
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:58,920
 Those things are not as quite conducive to husbandry.

171
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:01,480
 So I knew I had to make a decision.

172
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,720
 And yet the reason I was able to make that decision,

173
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:08,720
 I was able to bend the knee by the ring, pop the question,

174
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:13,300
 was because I realized something important.

175
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:19,260
 That I did want all of Brooke.

176
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:25,160
 But that meant I had to give all of me.

177
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:30,040
 That was my decision.

178
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,320
 And the truth of the matter is a lot of you

179
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,000
 are facing a similar decision today,

180
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,400
 like you've been in a relationship with Jesus

181
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,160
 where, man, you've made amazing memories.

182
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,280
 Like you have shared some incredible laughs,

183
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,440
 you've gotten to know each other,

184
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:44,240
 you've listened to him by way of his word,

185
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:46,560
 you've talked to him by way of your prayers,

186
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:51,120
 you've experienced his family as you come into his church,

187
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,820
 you've learned everything that he has in store

188
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:56,080
 for not only your life, but for the rest of the world.

189
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,560
 You've learned his dreams and his hopes and his aims.

190
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:01,320
 And yet, though you know each other so well,

191
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:04,220
 you have not made the decision to go all the way with him.

192
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:06,440
 Because yeah, you've got Jesus,

193
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:09,340
 but you've also got your career, and you've got your friends,

194
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:11,700
 and you've got your hobbies, and you've got your influence,

195
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,720
 and you've got your followers, and you've got your body,

196
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,320
 and you've got your reputation to keep,

197
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:17,680
 and you've got your dreams and your own aspirations,

198
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,680
 things that you are desperate to achieve,

199
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:20,960
 none of which are the problem.

200
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:24,520
 Like the problem is not that you want all of the things,

201
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:28,880
 the problem is that you want Jesus,

202
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,760
 you just don't want surrender.

203
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:34,120
 Which as I say that,

204
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,920
 I know some of you are probably thinking to yourself,

205
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:38,600
 he must be talking about somebody else down the row,

206
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,560
 sitting next to me even, because you know your story,

207
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:44,920
 you know your habits, you know the schedule of your life

208
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:47,460
 is that you show up to church on Sundays,

209
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:50,520
 you get in quiet times over the course of your week,

210
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:53,400
 you show up on Tuesday nights or stream along with us,

211
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,960
 you know that you post the occasional Bible verse,

212
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,760
 and you don't get drunk, only buzzed.

213
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:02,800
 But there's the danger, you can look all the way in

214
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,960
 while still being one foot out.

215
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,280
 You can be sitting in the church with your Bible open,

216
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:10,840
 but you can have your heart checked out.

217
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,600
 You can sing all the lyrics,

218
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:15,640
 but you can never actually mean any of the words,

219
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:17,160
 you can take good notes,

220
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,840
 but you never actually apply them to your life

221
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:21,360
 so that way they live out loud.

222
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:24,160
 You see, you can love Jesus sincerely,

223
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:27,520
 and still refuse to surrender completely.

224
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:31,600
 But here's the thing, that's not what Christ

225
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,040
 came to give you, Christ did not come to give you

226
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:40,280
 this sort of life where you are torn between two spaces.

227
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:44,880
 Him and you, he came to give you a life

228
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:48,640
 that requires all of you, and the reason we know it

229
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,440
 is because it required all of him, he went first,

230
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:54,680
 and so now we give all of ourselves in response.

231
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:57,120
 He has called you to a life of surrender,

232
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,800
 and what I wanna do is I wanna talk to you

233
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:01,160
 about some steps you can take to actually do that,

234
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:04,160
 because in rooms like this, in times like these,

235
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,920
 it's easy for us to talk about the merits of surrender,

236
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,560
 and to even feel like we've done it a time or two,

237
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:12,240
 and yet what we realize is this is a decision

238
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,600
 that we are continually faced.

239
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:18,120
 It's interesting, it's said that the average adult

240
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:23,120
 makes 35,000 decisions a day, most of which don't matter.

241
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:26,480
 Most of those decisions are immaterial,

242
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,760
 those are decisions like should I drink out

243
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,880
 of this coffee mug or that coffee mug?

244
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:31,240
 Should I text that friend back,

245
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:34,480
 or should I wait until another more opportune time to do so?

246
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:37,000
 Should I go out with my friends, or should I stay home?

247
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,360
 Should I stay in that line of the grocery store

248
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,600
 or that line, which inevitably always ends up

249
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,360
 being the wrong one, you know, you pick that

250
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,760
 whenever that situation happens.

251
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:47,600
 We always make thousands of immaterial decisions a day,

252
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:50,040
 and yet there are times in life

253
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:52,400
 when you're handed a really big one,

254
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,880
 and in your young adult years, you get hit

255
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,160
 with more of these than at any other point in your life,

256
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:58,120
 in your 20s and 30s, you are faced

257
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,200
 with so many of these decisions.

258
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,240
 Where will you go to school?

259
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,080
 What will you study, grad program or not?

260
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,920
 Who will your friends be?

261
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:04,760
 Will you keep up with those friends?

262
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,280
 Maybe you should make new friends.

263
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,120
 Where will you live?

264
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:07,960
 Who will you live with?

265
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:10,920
 Do you take a job in Dallas, or do you move to Denver?

266
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,360
 Do you go on a date?

267
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,040
 Should you go on a second date, a third date?

268
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,120
 Maybe we should have a DTR,

269
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,440
 because we've been dating for quite a while.

270
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,560
 Oh my gosh, we're in a relationship.

271
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:18,800
 I didn't know that we were in a relationship.

272
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,840
 I thought we were just dating,

273
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,880
 but now this has gotten serious.

274
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,080
 Should we get married?

275
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:24,400
 Do we have kids?

276
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,240
 How many kids?

277
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:26,080
 Home school?

278
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:26,920
 Nah.

279
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:27,760
 Private school?

280
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,600
 Public school.

281
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,960
 Do we move back near family,

282
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,080
 or can we do this thing on our own?

283
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,440
 And it goes on and on and on,

284
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,240
 because in your stage of life,

285
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,960
 there are so many decisions demanded of you,

286
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,280
 and yet here's what I would say.

287
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:42,520
 Though your 20s and 30s feel like a series of pop quizzes

288
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:45,160
 that you never got the opportunity to study for,

289
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:48,520
 there is not one decision,

290
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:51,720
 but a decision every single day

291
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:55,000
 that you must make continually for the rest of your life,

292
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,200
 because yes, it is true.

293
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:58,840
 In most cases with big decisions,

294
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,760
 they are relatively rare,

295
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:04,600
 and they happen maybe once, maybe twice,

296
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,080
 and yet the truth of the matter is,

297
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,560
 the most important decision you can make in your life,

298
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,240
 the biggest decision that you will make,

299
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,840
 is not a once in a lifetime kind of choice.

300
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:17,520
 It is an every day, day by day,

301
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:19,160
 even on your worst day,

302
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:22,000
 until the day you die kind of decision,

303
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,080
 and it's this.

304
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:27,160
 Will you go all in with Jesus?

305
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,480
 Will you go all in with him?

306
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:32,280
 Because that's what Paul is talking about

307
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,080
 in the book of Romans.

308
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,840
 If you have a Bible, turn with me to Romans chapter 12.

309
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,600
 While you're doing that,

310
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:41,720
 we're catching the book of Romans at its hinge point.

311
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,640
 You see chapters one through 11,

312
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,040
 unpack for us all the glories of the gospel.

313
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:48,800
 It tells us about who God is, who Christ is,

314
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:51,320
 what Christ has come to do in light of who we are

315
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:52,560
 and what we needed,

316
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,480
 and because he has done all of that,

317
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:57,360
 we find ourselves in chapter 12 to the end of the book,

318
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,720
 considering what now is the product of our life.

319
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:01,760
 So here's what's important.

320
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:02,920
 You cannot consider anything

321
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:05,200
 that we're going to talk about tonight together

322
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,760
 if you do not first and foremost,

323
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,120
 have a relationship with Jesus.

324
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:10,040
 Paul is even gonna open up this chapter

325
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,680
 by talking to brothers.

326
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:12,680
 That's brothers and sisters,

327
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:15,480
 meaning people that are within the family of God,

328
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,440
 and yet he wants to unpack for us

329
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,360
 some very important principles that we need,

330
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,680
 so that way we understand what it looks like

331
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:24,080
 to take legitimate steps towards surrender.

332
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,560
 So here's what he says in Romans 12.

333
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,440
 We're just gonna look at two verses.

334
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,880
 Says this in verse one,

335
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:31,160
 "I appeal to you therefore, brothers,

336
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,460
 "by the mercies of God,

337
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:34,600
 "to present your bodies as a living sacrifice,

338
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,300
 "holy and acceptable to God,

339
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:38,080
 "which is your spiritual worship.

340
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:40,440
 "Do not be conformed to this world,

341
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:43,200
 "but be transformed by the renewal of your mind,

342
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:45,620
 "that by testing you may discern what is the will of God,

343
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:49,280
 "what is good and acceptable and perfect."

344
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,840
 So how do you give your all to Jesus?

345
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,920
 How do you actually surrender yourself to him?

346
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:57,800
 Well, in order to understand that,

347
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:00,800
 you have to understand something about sacrifices.

348
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:02,180
 Probably didn't see that coming,

349
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:05,080
 but that's what Paul is unpacking in Romans 12, one and two.

350
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,520
 He is talking to your life now

351
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,480
 on the other side of the cross,

352
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,240
 having professed your faith in Jesus,

353
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:12,680
 and standing with him today,

354
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,960
 and journeying with him through the rest of your life.

355
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,280
 He is looking at you and he is saying,

356
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:19,360
 "Hey, your life is to now, forever,

357
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:22,120
 "and always be known as a living sacrifice."

358
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,280
 Which means we've gotta understand

359
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,720
 some things about sacrifices.

360
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,400
 What do we need to understand about sacrifices?

361
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,080
 We, I did this on Tuesday.

362
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,840
 What we have to know about sacrifices is,

363
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:33,980
 number one, that we offer ourselves entirely.

364
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:35,720
 You gotta offer yourself entirely.

365
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:39,240
 Because here's the thing, in the Old Testament,

366
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,640
 burnt offerings, which is what Paul

367
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:43,140
 is specifically talking about

368
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:45,660
 when he describes living sacrifices.

369
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:50,460
 Burnt offerings, they were the only whole offering

370
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:53,860
 that the people of God gave.

371
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:57,420
 Whole offering, meaning there was nothing left

372
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:58,280
 for leftovers.

373
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:01,100
 It was the whole thing offered at a single time.

374
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,620
 We see it over the course of Scripture.

375
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:04,300
 It says in Deuteronomy 33, 10,

376
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:07,100
 "They shall teach Jacob your rules, and Israel your law.

377
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,640
 "They shall put incense before you,

378
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:12,220
 "and whole burnt offerings on your altar."

379
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:15,060
 Psalm 51, 19 says, "Then will you delight

380
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:17,280
 "in right sacrifices, and burnt offerings,

381
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:19,060
 "and whole burnt offerings.

382
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:21,380
 "Then bulls will be offered on your altar."

383
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:26,100
 Exodus 29, 18 says, "And burn the whole ram on the altar."

384
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:27,900
 It is a burnt offering to the Lord.

385
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:31,060
 It is a pleasing aroma of food offering to the Lord.

386
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:32,280
 I could give you more, but hopefully

387
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,340
 that gets the message across.

388
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:35,860
 Burnt offering is a whole offering,

389
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:39,080
 which means it is offered entirely.

390
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:41,700
 When it comes to your life as an offering to God,

391
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:44,380
 He doesn't just want half of you.

392
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:46,140
 He doesn't want some of you.

393
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:47,700
 He doesn't want most of you.

394
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:52,700
 He wants all of you, the entirety of who you are.

395
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,820
 When Paul says, "Present your body,"

396
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:59,420
 that word body literally means the complete totality

397
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:04,040
 of whoever you are, like the whole of you right now

398
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,700
 in this room as you are,

399
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,340
 even if you wish things were different.

400
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:10,260
 Like He wants the things that you pride yourself on at work,

401
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:12,920
 the things that you conceal when you look in the mirror,

402
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,860
 the things that you committed to doing this year,

403
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:16,740
 and the things that you failed to do this year,

404
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:18,180
 the things that you joke about with your friends,

405
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:20,160
 the things that you regret when you think about your past,

406
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:21,820
 the thing you refuse to tell anyone else.

407
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:25,140
 He wants all of it, all of it.

408
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:29,120
 That's why Paul uses the word present.

409
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:34,060
 It's interesting, that word present carries the idea

410
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:38,780
 of bestowing upon somebody something else,

411
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:41,700
 bestowing upon somebody something that you have.

412
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:43,420
 And it doesn't mean that it comes

413
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,360
 from a place of swagger or pride.

414
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,620
 There's no ego involved.

415
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:49,140
 It's not like now presenting best living sacrifice.

416
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,380
 That's not the idea here.

417
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:53,300
 The idea instead is birth and humility,

418
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:56,460
 because when you consider what present actually means,

419
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:58,320
 it means to hand something over to someone

420
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,380
 of superior status or rank.

421
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,420
 It comes from a place of humility.

422
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:04,340
 So I remember when I graduated college,

423
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:07,580
 like some of you in the room, I graduated with debt.

424
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:10,540
 And the reason why is because college is expensive.

425
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:12,540
 I did my best, had some scholarships,

426
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:14,380
 tried to earn grants, and even worked

427
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:15,380
 to make some money on the side.

428
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:16,220
 And yet at the end of the day,

429
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:20,100
 I walked out with some debt in my name.

430
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:23,500
 And so I graduated and started to work a full-time job.

431
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:24,420
 And yet somewhere along the way,

432
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:26,100
 I remember my dad sitting me down.

433
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:28,740
 And as he sat with me, he just asked,

434
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:30,740
 hey man, I don't wanna be invasive,

435
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:33,380
 but would you be cool if we opened up your bank account

436
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,900
 and we looked specifically at the debt

437
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:35,940
 that you owe from school?

438
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:38,100
 And I was like, sure, man, like,

439
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,500
 it doesn't bother me if we look at it together.

440
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,340
 And so we opened up my debt,

441
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:42,740
 and then he proceeded to ask me,

442
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:46,020
 hey, would you let me have that?

443
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:50,660
 Would you give me all of the debt that is left to you?

444
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:55,620
 And I remember in that moment feeling so humbled.

445
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:56,740
 I wasn't proud.

446
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:58,340
 It's like, about time you recognized.

447
00:17:58,340 --> 00:18:00,680
 That would have been the most inappropriate response.

448
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:01,520
 Why?

449
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:02,700
 Because it wasn't his fault.

450
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:06,340
 It was my fault, and yet he was making it his problem.

451
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:08,540
 He wanted to take it onto himself,

452
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:11,140
 but it required me present it to him,

453
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:15,260
 offer it to him, give it over to him.

454
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,760
 And he was of superior rank to myself.

455
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,420
 He actually was better suited

456
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:20,740
 to handle the issue than I was.

457
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,500
 Now, as I say that, some of you are sitting here

458
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:24,380
 thinking to yourself, yeah, man,

459
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:27,020
 I would totally present a problem to God,

460
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:28,500
 but this isn't necessarily just talking

461
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:29,340
 about giving him my problems.

462
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:31,860
 This is talking about giving him myself, my whole life.

463
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,420
 And yet the truth of the matter is,

464
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:37,740
 the disbelief that Jesus deserves your all

465
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,900
 actually implies the belief that you think

466
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:43,300
 satisfaction is found someplace else, and it's not.

467
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:46,100
 He is asking you to give him all of yourself,

468
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,020
 the good and the bad.

469
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:47,840
 Why?

470
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:49,460
 Because he knows as you present it to him,

471
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:50,980
 he will be able to return to you

472
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:52,580
 what you have actually wanted for,

473
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,820
 which is genuine satisfaction.

474
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:58,540
 You see, we're called to surrender everything to Jesus,

475
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:01,100
 and yet that's the issue for so many of us in here.

476
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:03,100
 We think we're surrendering our lives to Jesus

477
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:06,160
 when we're really just sharing our lives with Jesus.

478
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:09,420
 Like, Jesus, you can have my Sunday mornings,

479
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:10,540
 you can have my Tuesday nights,

480
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:12,700
 and I'll even give you my Wednesday nights

481
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:13,900
 'cause we got a group at that time,

482
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:16,380
 and maybe a 20-minute devotional in the morning,

483
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:19,420
 but I need to keep Monday afternoon happy hour

484
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:22,540
 because Monday's tough and the rest of the week's coming,

485
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:24,300
 and I need to just unwind a little bit, you know?

486
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:27,300
 Or my favorite show, it airs every Thursday night,

487
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:28,260
 so maybe I can keep that one

488
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:29,680
 'cause I really wanna keep up with that show.

489
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,900
 It's about to drop, and I need to make sure

490
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:32,860
 that I'm tuning in alongside, or maybe it's not that,

491
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:34,460
 maybe it's Friday night, I've got softball league,

492
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,580
 and so we've actually got a chance to win this year,

493
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:37,940
 and they need me, man, I gotta show up,

494
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:38,880
 and I gotta be a part of it.

495
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:40,460
 Every weekend, those are for my friends,

496
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:41,700
 so Jesus, you can have some of this,

497
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:43,380
 but you can't have the rest of this.

498
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:46,060
 Now, hear me on this, I just want you to know,

499
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:49,100
 I'm not villainizing any of those things

500
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,820
 because the truth of the matter is, in the Christian life,

501
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:52,540
 it's not all fasting.

502
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:53,860
 There is some feasting involved.

503
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:56,100
 Like, there should be the genuine enjoyment

504
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,660
 of things that we've just described,

505
00:19:57,660 --> 00:20:02,140
 and yet the reality is, the more of yourself you give away,

506
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,260
 the less of yourself you have to offer,

507
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:06,580
 and so this weekend, there's gonna be a chance

508
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:09,760
 for some of you to take yourself back

509
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,460
 so you can give yourself to God

510
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,700
 to actually offer all of who you are to him

511
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:16,500
 because that's what he wants.

512
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,580
 You see, we live in a world

513
00:20:18,580 --> 00:20:20,300
 that has branded following Jesus

514
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:22,500
 with a calculated sort of devotion,

515
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:25,140
 a cultural Christianity that many of you are aware of,

516
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:27,300
 a celebritized sort of faith

517
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:30,580
 that says Jesus is fine with whatever you wanna give,

518
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:33,940
 to which I wanna say no!

519
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:35,780
 No one is in a position,

520
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:38,420
 no one finds himself in a relationship

521
00:20:38,420 --> 00:20:40,420
 with someone they love that's like,

522
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:42,260
 he loves me most of the time,

523
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:44,200
 but some of the time, he loves somebody else.

524
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,460
 Nobody would have any sort of interest in that.

525
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:48,180
 It's funny, I've even, I've read the article,

526
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:50,020
 I've talked to people in open relationships,

527
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:53,020
 polyamorous relationships, and they all, in the same way,

528
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:55,340
 even if they advocate that that is best,

529
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,620
 the truth of the matter is

530
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,940
 they always end with people jealous.

531
00:20:58,940 --> 00:20:59,780
 Why?

532
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:02,960
 Because nobody wants to share their beloved's affection.

533
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:03,800
 Guess what?

534
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,320
 Your God is jealous too.

535
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:08,660
 Your God is a jealous God.

536
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:10,640
 Exodus 20, verses four and five says,

537
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:14,420
 "You shall not make for yourself a carved image

538
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:17,300
 "or any likeness of anything that is heaven above

539
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:19,400
 "or that which is in the earth beneath

540
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:21,660
 "or that is in the water under the earth.

541
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:24,800
 "You shall not bow down to them or serve them

542
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:27,780
 "for I, the Lord your God, I'm a jealous God."

543
00:21:27,780 --> 00:21:29,580
 So hear me on this.

544
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:31,460
 What does it mean that God is a jealous God?

545
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:33,380
 It means that God will not be king at all

546
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:34,940
 if he cannot be king of all.

547
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:41,660
 God will not be king at all if he cannot be king of all.

548
00:21:41,660 --> 00:21:48,980
 That's why the offering is consumed completely.

549
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:51,900
 It is offered whole.

550
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:54,840
 And we should be too.

551
00:21:54,840 --> 00:22:00,100
 So let me ask you, what have you withheld from the altar?

552
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:03,500
 If your life is meant to be lived on the altar,

553
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:06,660
 living sacrifice unto God, what have you withheld from him?

554
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:10,860
 And I don't ask that in a condemning way.

555
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:13,380
 I don't ask that in an attempt to guilt you.

556
00:22:13,380 --> 00:22:18,280
 I ask that in a way to release you, to free you,

557
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:24,400
 to invite you into the sort of wholehearted devotion

558
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:27,920
 that Christ went to the cross to give you.

559
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:31,340
 So what have you withheld from the altar?

560
00:22:31,340 --> 00:22:33,880
 Is it your relationship?

561
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:37,140
 Is it your health?

562
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,700
 Is it your family?

563
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:43,180
 Is it your career?

564
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:46,500
 I get it, I talk to people all the time down here.

565
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:48,220
 They'll come up and they'll talk to me about

566
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:50,040
 a relationship that they dearly love

567
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:52,260
 and yet they know there's something about the relationship

568
00:22:52,260 --> 00:22:54,740
 that isn't quite right.

569
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:56,540
 And yet they're willing to compromise on that relationship

570
00:22:56,540 --> 00:22:57,980
 because they want to be loved.

571
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,780
 And in the process of doing so, they dismiss the fact

572
00:22:59,780 --> 00:23:02,020
 that they already have been loved.

573
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:03,860
 And the one who loves them has so much more for them

574
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:06,420
 than they actually want for themselves.

575
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:08,540
 Or I'll talk to people that will visit with me

576
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:10,240
 about their families.

577
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,340
 That will look at me and will tell me about

578
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:16,160
 marriages that are a mess between their parents

579
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:18,680
 or siblings that have just gone rogue

580
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:21,880
 or generational sin that has abounded for so very long

581
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:23,600
 and yet despite all of their effort

582
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:25,600
 and all of the prayers they've prayed

583
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,040
 and all the times that they've shared,

584
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:30,520
 it feels like God never actually shows up.

585
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:32,640
 And yet what they've done is they've counted out a God

586
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:35,280
 that has never failed to be faithful to his promises.

587
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:38,480
 Or it's in people's career.

588
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:41,520
 They got big dreams.

589
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:43,420
 They want to be a millionaire by 25.

590
00:23:43,420 --> 00:23:44,260
 Me too.

591
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,760
 And yet in the process of doing so,

592
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:50,840
 they're willing to make genuine compromises

593
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:52,200
 that forego their convictions

594
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:54,440
 because that's what it takes to sit in the halls of power

595
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:56,360
 and at the table of influence.

596
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:58,040
 And yet as they do so, they forget the fact

597
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,640
 that they've already been bestowed

598
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:01,280
 with an immense amount of approval

599
00:24:01,280 --> 00:24:03,080
 and they need not worry about anything

600
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:05,560
 because if he so clothes the field,

601
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:07,160
 will he not much more clothe you?

602
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:10,040
 If he so feeds the birds, will he not much more feed you?

603
00:24:10,040 --> 00:24:12,920
 We do this.

604
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:16,440
 We withhold from the altar.

605
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:17,680
 But here's the thing.

606
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:19,480
 Tonight,

607
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:24,000
 we can put it all on the altar.

608
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:28,300
 We can offer ourselves entirely.

609
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:32,680
 I visit with people often who tell me

610
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:33,880
 they're so burnt out on Christ

611
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,640
 and the truth of the matter is they have burnt out

612
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:38,080
 because they've never actually burned up.

613
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:40,120
 They never gave all of themselves to God.

614
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:42,600
 Why wouldn't you?

615
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:45,680
 Why wouldn't you give all of yourselves to God?

616
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:47,880
 Only you know the answer for that.

617
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:50,240
 I've got ideas of why that might be

618
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:51,520
 because you love Love Island

619
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,080
 and you don't know that you could ever go a day without it

620
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:54,560
 but maybe you should go a day without it

621
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:56,180
 or you think about your life

622
00:24:56,180 --> 00:24:57,900
 and you consider the friends that you spend time with

623
00:24:57,900 --> 00:24:59,560
 and man, you don't wanna break those friendships

624
00:24:59,560 --> 00:25:00,400
 and yet the truth of the matter is

625
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:01,480
 you probably should break those friendships

626
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:02,560
 because there's plenty of people out there

627
00:25:02,560 --> 00:25:03,500
 and they're better friends.

628
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:04,560
 In fact, to find that those friends

629
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:06,440
 are asking you to compromise your convictions in Christ.

630
00:25:06,440 --> 00:25:07,880
 There's so many things that I could tell you

631
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:12,080
 but you know why you're actually,

632
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:14,960
 why you're actually not giving all of yourself to Jesus,

633
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:16,720
 why you're not going the whole way.

634
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:19,480
 So let me just ask you,

635
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:21,320
 instead of begging the question,

636
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:23,360
 how far do I need to go, Kylan?

637
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:27,840
 What if you asked instead, how far can I go, Kylan?

638
00:25:27,840 --> 00:25:30,600
 How much can I do?

639
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:34,200
 What would it look like to be the most radical person

640
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:39,200
 in this room as opposed to calculate my devotion any longer?

641
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:42,760
 You see, Christ lived that way.

642
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:43,920
 He went the whole way.

643
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:48,580
 You see, he did it because he knew

644
00:25:48,580 --> 00:25:50,960
 in order to present a sacrifice to God,

645
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:52,660
 what had to be true of that sacrifice?

646
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:55,240
 That sacrifice had to be spotless.

647
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:57,120
 It had to be guiltless.

648
00:25:57,120 --> 00:26:00,000
 It had to be completely blameless, unblemished

649
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:02,040
 and the truth of the matter is not a single person

650
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:03,800
 in this room apart from Christ

651
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:06,160
 can say that that is true of who they are.

652
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:09,560
 Every one of us is marred by sin.

653
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:12,080
 The stain goes so very deep

654
00:26:12,080 --> 00:26:13,840
 and no matter how hard we try to clean,

655
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,600
 it cannot be removed

656
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:18,280
 and yet the only way we can present ourselves

657
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:20,720
 the whole of who we are as an unblemished sacrifice

658
00:26:20,720 --> 00:26:22,040
 is through Christ.

659
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:23,080
 How did he do it?

660
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:26,480
 By offering the entirety of who he is

661
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:28,040
 so that way we might be made clean

662
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:31,040
 and we could do so likewise in response.

663
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:32,920
 Friends, offer yourself entirely

664
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:35,160
 because Christ has offered himself entirely.

665
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,360
 That's the first step of surrender.

666
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:39,040
 The second step is you have to offer yourself

667
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:41,000
 consistently.

668
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,840
 You offer yourself consistently

669
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:44,520
 which sounds crazy, right?

670
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,360
 Consistently.

671
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:46,180
 What do we mean by that?

672
00:26:46,180 --> 00:26:47,200
 Once a week?

673
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:48,240
 Twice a week?

674
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,080
 Three times a week?

675
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:51,000
 No, every single day, every single moment

676
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,120
 for the rest of your life.

677
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:54,520
 That sounds insane.

678
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:56,320
 That sounds crazy.

679
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:57,640
 Who would even do that?

680
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:58,480
 You wanna know who does that?

681
00:26:58,480 --> 00:26:59,480
 Christians do that.

682
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:03,200
 It sounds crazy but whoever said you were called

683
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,560
 to a normal kind of life?

684
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:08,600
 You offer yourself consistently.

685
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:11,840
 Leviticus six verses eight through nine says,

686
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:14,040
 "The Lord spoke to Moses saying,

687
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,760
 "Command Aaron and his son saying,

688
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:17,660
 "this is the law of the burnt offering.

689
00:27:17,660 --> 00:27:20,280
 "The burnt offering shall be on the hearth

690
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:23,160
 "on the altar all night until the morning

691
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:26,280
 "and the fire of the altar shall be kept burning on it."

692
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:27,400
 Verse 12.

693
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:30,040
 "The fire on the altar shall be kept burning on it.

694
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:32,280
 "It shall not go out.

695
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:34,880
 "The priest shall burn wood on it every morning

696
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:36,880
 "and he shall arrange the burnt offering on it

697
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:39,200
 "and shall burn on it the fat of the peace offerings.

698
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:42,200
 "Fire shall be kept burning on the altar continually.

699
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:43,600
 "It shall not go out."

700
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,560
 Why shouldn't it go out?

701
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:47,400
 Because this is no ordinary fire.

702
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:50,480
 This is holy fire.

703
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:52,560
 It's interesting, when you study fire in the Bible,

704
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:55,120
 what you realize is fire is representative

705
00:27:55,120 --> 00:27:56,120
 of the presence of God.

706
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:57,920
 You see it in the life of Abraham

707
00:27:57,920 --> 00:27:59,240
 as he covenants with God.

708
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:02,280
 God is represented as a flaming torch in a smoking pot.

709
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:05,960
 You see it whenever Moses encounters the burning bush.

710
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:08,880
 God's presence is in the bush

711
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:11,520
 that is ablaze and yet not burned up.

712
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:13,760
 You see it as the Israelites make their way

713
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:15,480
 through the wilderness out of Egypt.

714
00:28:15,480 --> 00:28:18,520
 They're led by a pillar of fire by night

715
00:28:18,520 --> 00:28:20,760
 and a cloud of smoke by day.

716
00:28:20,760 --> 00:28:23,080
 And then you see it whenever they get to Mount Sinai,

717
00:28:23,080 --> 00:28:24,920
 Mount Sinai, which means Mount Fire.

718
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:26,240
 And when they get to Mount Sinai,

719
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:28,120
 what is the mountain wrapped within?

720
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:31,520
 It is wrapped in smoke and fire.

721
00:28:31,520 --> 00:28:34,680
 God's presence is represented by fire.

722
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:37,840
 And not just that, God himself identifies as such.

723
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:38,920
 Deuteronomy 4, 24 says,

724
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:43,920
 "For the Lord your God is a consuming fire, a jealous God."

725
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:47,440
 Fire is always representative of God's presence.

726
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:51,600
 And what's fascinating is that when you look at the times,

727
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:54,120
 when the places, the tabernacle, the temple,

728
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:56,960
 and the people of God are erected

729
00:28:56,960 --> 00:28:59,680
 to receive the presence of God in their lives,

730
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,800
 what is his presence represented as?

731
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,280
 Fire.

732
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:06,480
 It literally falls from heaven

733
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:08,960
 and it comes down here to earth.

734
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:11,640
 Every time, it's fire that fills the place

735
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:13,960
 because the presence of God fills that place,

736
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:16,440
 which is really kind of God if you think about it.

737
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:20,000
 Because anyone knows, particularly those survival experts,

738
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:24,200
 that the hardest part of fire building in the open world

739
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,960
 is always the process of getting the fire started.

740
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:29,600
 I don't know if you've ever tried it.

741
00:29:29,600 --> 00:29:33,000
 Just like no materials, no light or fluid, that's cheating.

742
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:36,760
 You and some sticks make fire.

743
00:29:36,760 --> 00:29:38,480
 It is impossibly difficult.

744
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:39,320
 Why?

745
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:42,960
 Because it requires so many variables to go right.

746
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:45,760
 Like you have to have like really dry kindling.

747
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:46,840
 And if you're in an environment

748
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:49,800
 that's extremely moist or windy,

749
00:29:49,800 --> 00:29:51,420
 then that makes it super difficult

750
00:29:51,420 --> 00:29:53,760
 because those things are not conducive to building fire.

751
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:55,240
 You gotta have the right amount of oxygen.

752
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:57,040
 Too much oxygen, it'll blow out.

753
00:29:57,040 --> 00:29:59,000
 Too little oxygen, it won't catch flame.

754
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,680
 And you need small enough fuel

755
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:02,000
 that you can add to the fire

756
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:03,320
 so that way when it begins to catch,

757
00:30:03,320 --> 00:30:04,800
 it has something small enough to catch on

758
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:05,640
 'cause you might smother it

759
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:07,520
 if you put too big an item upon it.

760
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:08,720
 It is a difficult process.

761
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:11,480
 It's the reason Tom Hanks goes ballistic

762
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:13,440
 whenever he makes it in "Castaway."

763
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:14,880
 You think you would do no different?

764
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,160
 Then I dare you try.

765
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:19,720
 It is so very hard, and yet it is kind of God to say,

766
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,200
 "I'll take care of that, everybody.

767
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:23,600
 "I will literally whoosh,

768
00:30:23,600 --> 00:30:27,040
 "blow up the altar with heavenly fire."

769
00:30:27,040 --> 00:30:31,240
 You wanna know what the easiest part of fire building is?

770
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:34,480
 Keeping it lit.

771
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:37,000
 That's our job.

772
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:40,280
 He sends the fire.

773
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:42,560
 We tend the flame.

774
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:46,280
 He has done the heavy lifting,

775
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:51,240
 and he has left the reasonable portion to us.

776
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:53,120
 How do you tend the flame, friends?

777
00:30:53,120 --> 00:30:56,960
 You stay on the altar

778
00:30:58,380 --> 00:31:01,620
 because as necessary as it is to commit your life to Christ

779
00:31:01,620 --> 00:31:02,540
 in a single moment,

780
00:31:02,540 --> 00:31:06,100
 it is equally necessary that we recommit our lives to Christ

781
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:07,740
 in every moment.

782
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:08,700
 Why is that?

783
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:11,020
 Because this isn't just about making yourself

784
00:31:11,020 --> 00:31:11,860
 right before God.

785
00:31:11,860 --> 00:31:13,060
 That's not what we're talking about.

786
00:31:13,060 --> 00:31:14,700
 Again, this is written to believers,

787
00:31:14,700 --> 00:31:16,780
 people that have placed their faith in Jesus.

788
00:31:16,780 --> 00:31:19,420
 We are not talking about you making yourself right

789
00:31:19,420 --> 00:31:20,420
 in the eyes of God.

790
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:23,260
 What we are talking about is you making God

791
00:31:23,260 --> 00:31:25,620
 right in the eyes of yourself.

792
00:31:25,620 --> 00:31:28,660
 This is about your perspective on God changing,

793
00:31:28,660 --> 00:31:33,320
 ever increasing, actually growing better.

794
00:31:33,320 --> 00:31:37,100
 So early in my life, I was a legit altar call.

795
00:31:37,100 --> 00:31:39,220
 Anybody else in the room, like that's how you came to faith,

796
00:31:39,220 --> 00:31:40,660
 was a legitimate altar call?

797
00:31:40,660 --> 00:31:42,220
 Nobody else, just me.

798
00:31:42,220 --> 00:31:45,780
 I was 14 years old, and I remember it like it was yesterday.

799
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:50,060
 I was at this youth retreat in a room way bigger than this

800
00:31:50,060 --> 00:31:52,100
 with thousands upon thousands of young,

801
00:31:52,100 --> 00:31:54,620
 with middle school and high school kids.

802
00:31:54,620 --> 00:31:59,260
 There was this cheesy 2000s youth skit happening on stage.

803
00:31:59,260 --> 00:32:01,580
 Literally, like there was a guy in a white bathrobe,

804
00:32:01,580 --> 00:32:03,820
 like pulling this girl with an imaginary rope

805
00:32:03,820 --> 00:32:05,500
 out of her sin and towards himself.

806
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:07,580
 And I looked at that and I was like, that's me.

807
00:32:07,580 --> 00:32:09,620
 Like, I've got to go and I've got to place my faith.

808
00:32:09,620 --> 00:32:11,800
 And I got up and I went down front

809
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:13,220
 and I surrendered my life to Jesus,

810
00:32:13,220 --> 00:32:15,900
 and it was the greatest decision I've ever made.

811
00:32:15,900 --> 00:32:17,300
 But here's the thing, listen to me.

812
00:32:17,300 --> 00:32:18,980
 (congregation applauding)

813
00:32:18,980 --> 00:32:21,420
 While that was the greatest decision I've ever made,

814
00:32:21,420 --> 00:32:24,620
 to commit my life on the altar that day,

815
00:32:24,620 --> 00:32:25,980
 an equally great decision,

816
00:32:25,980 --> 00:32:30,060
 is to recommit my life on the altar every single day,

817
00:32:30,060 --> 00:32:32,260
 that I might continue to walk with my Jesus,

818
00:32:32,260 --> 00:32:33,540
 not one foot in, one foot out,

819
00:32:33,540 --> 00:32:35,180
 but both the all the way in,

820
00:32:35,180 --> 00:32:36,540
 in the direction that he is heading.

821
00:32:36,540 --> 00:32:39,060
 Life with him is better than life at its best.

822
00:32:39,060 --> 00:32:40,760
 I want to go where he is going.

823
00:32:40,760 --> 00:32:43,100
 Do you want to do the same?

824
00:32:43,100 --> 00:32:45,140
 Because here's the tricky thing about living sacrifices.

825
00:32:45,140 --> 00:32:46,660
 Are you listening to me?

826
00:32:46,660 --> 00:32:48,300
 They want to crawl off the altar.

827
00:32:50,140 --> 00:32:53,060
 Living sacrifices want to crawl off the altar.

828
00:32:53,060 --> 00:32:55,260
 They do not want to stay there.

829
00:32:55,260 --> 00:32:57,540
 So every day we have to make the decision

830
00:32:57,540 --> 00:32:59,740
 to surrender to Christ, to surrender to Christ,

831
00:32:59,740 --> 00:33:00,780
 to trust his ways and not our own,

832
00:33:00,780 --> 00:33:02,140
 to trust his truth and not our own,

833
00:33:02,140 --> 00:33:03,580
 to trust his plans and not our own.

834
00:33:03,580 --> 00:33:06,540
 Because when we don't, when we crawl off the altar,

835
00:33:06,540 --> 00:33:08,340
 when we stop tending the fire,

836
00:33:08,340 --> 00:33:10,900
 when we become inattentive to God's presence,

837
00:33:10,900 --> 00:33:12,100
 guess what the cost is?

838
00:33:12,100 --> 00:33:14,920
 You become unaware of God's presence in your life.

839
00:33:17,020 --> 00:33:20,420
 You begin to put the fire out.

840
00:33:20,420 --> 00:33:22,140
 Now, I don't want to endanger you.

841
00:33:22,140 --> 00:33:23,860
 You're not at risk of losing your salvation,

842
00:33:23,860 --> 00:33:28,820
 but you are at risk of losing your sensitivity to his spirit.

843
00:33:28,820 --> 00:33:32,260
 That's why Paul says in 1 Thessalonians 5, verses 19 to 21,

844
00:33:32,260 --> 00:33:34,260
 he says, "Do not quench the spirit."

845
00:33:34,260 --> 00:33:35,140
 Do you hear it?

846
00:33:35,140 --> 00:33:36,180
 Don't quench the spirit.

847
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:37,940
 That's fire language.

848
00:33:37,940 --> 00:33:39,980
 Don't despise prophecies, but test everything.

849
00:33:39,980 --> 00:33:41,860
 Hold fast what is good.

850
00:33:41,860 --> 00:33:44,000
 Why does he use fire language in this moment?

851
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:45,540
 Don't quench the spirit,

852
00:33:45,540 --> 00:33:48,300
 because he knows there are two ways

853
00:33:48,300 --> 00:33:49,220
 in which you can put a fire out.

854
00:33:49,220 --> 00:33:50,660
 Yes, you can walk up and you can just dump

855
00:33:50,660 --> 00:33:51,940
 a bucket of water on it.

856
00:33:51,940 --> 00:33:55,700
 But most typically, the way that fires go out

857
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:56,760
 is through neglect.

858
00:33:56,760 --> 00:34:01,500
 They're neglected until what was once a bright

859
00:34:01,500 --> 00:34:04,260
 and a burning flame becomes a small,

860
00:34:04,260 --> 00:34:06,300
 smoldering set of embers.

861
00:34:06,300 --> 00:34:10,180
 We must do everything in our power

862
00:34:10,180 --> 00:34:12,940
 to ensure we do not neglect him.

863
00:34:13,820 --> 00:34:15,460
 Because the cost of one mismourning

864
00:34:15,460 --> 00:34:17,760
 or one compromised conviction or one more excuse

865
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:21,760
 or one unconfessed sin is more detrimental than we realize.

866
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:27,900
 That's why Paul says in this chapter in Romans 12,

867
00:34:27,900 --> 00:34:31,100
 he says, "Don't be conformed to the world."

868
00:34:31,100 --> 00:34:35,500
 Because he knows if you're not being intentionally shaped

869
00:34:35,500 --> 00:34:38,900
 by Christ, you will be inevitably shaped by something else.

870
00:34:38,900 --> 00:34:41,540
 Either Christ will intentionally shape you

871
00:34:41,540 --> 00:34:44,500
 or something else will inevitably shape you.

872
00:34:44,500 --> 00:34:46,780
 The difference in being conformed and transformed

873
00:34:46,780 --> 00:34:50,340
 is conformed is I am changed by the pressures

874
00:34:50,340 --> 00:34:51,360
 outside of me.

875
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:57,520
 To be transformed is to be changed by the power within me.

876
00:34:57,520 --> 00:35:01,500
 There's a power within you known as the Holy Spirit.

877
00:35:01,500 --> 00:35:03,100
 It's not an it, it is a he.

878
00:35:03,100 --> 00:35:06,400
 He is a person of the Godhead and he wants to shape you.

879
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,420
 He wants to mold you.

880
00:35:07,420 --> 00:35:09,540
 He wants to change you, conform you,

881
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:12,300
 or he should transform you into the image of his son.

882
00:35:12,300 --> 00:35:15,340
 And yet the truth of the matter is,

883
00:35:15,340 --> 00:35:18,060
 you've got to stay on the altar for it to happen.

884
00:35:18,060 --> 00:35:20,500
 So let me ask you, have you crawled off the altar?

885
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:22,980
 Have you crawled off the altar?

886
00:35:22,980 --> 00:35:24,480
 Like if so, what for?

887
00:35:24,480 --> 00:35:27,860
 Tim Keller was the one who talked to us

888
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:31,580
 about four primary idols that all people succumb to.

889
00:35:31,580 --> 00:35:35,140
 The desire for power, a desire for approval,

890
00:35:35,140 --> 00:35:37,560
 a desire for comfort, a desire for control.

891
00:35:38,620 --> 00:35:41,100
 You will crawl off the altar for one of those.

892
00:35:41,100 --> 00:35:43,500
 And the truth of the matter is,

893
00:35:43,500 --> 00:35:45,260
 every one of us will crawl off

894
00:35:45,260 --> 00:35:47,780
 for each of those at some point.

895
00:35:47,780 --> 00:35:50,680
 The question is, which one have you crawled off for today?

896
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:55,700
 The minute you identify it is the minute you're able

897
00:35:55,700 --> 00:35:59,940
 to repent of it and come back to the altar.

898
00:35:59,940 --> 00:36:02,900
 You're able to cease quenching the fire

899
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:07,180
 and you can do what Paul tells his protege Timothy

900
00:36:07,180 --> 00:36:09,540
 later on, fan into flame the gift of God

901
00:36:09,540 --> 00:36:11,880
 that is in you through the laying on of my hands.

902
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:15,220
 Some of you, you need to fan into flame tonight.

903
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:16,860
 You got to get back on the altar.

904
00:36:16,860 --> 00:36:20,940
 And the final step of surrender

905
00:36:20,940 --> 00:36:23,360
 is that you offer yourself willingly.

906
00:36:23,360 --> 00:36:25,060
 You offer yourself willingly.

907
00:36:25,060 --> 00:36:28,340
 Because a truly surrendered life is not coerced.

908
00:36:28,340 --> 00:36:31,260
 It's volunteered.

909
00:36:31,260 --> 00:36:32,720
 It's volunteered.

910
00:36:32,720 --> 00:36:34,180
 You see it from the very first words.

911
00:36:34,180 --> 00:36:35,660
 I appeal to you.

912
00:36:35,660 --> 00:36:36,660
 I love that.

913
00:36:36,660 --> 00:36:38,780
 The word there in Greek that Paul is using

914
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:41,220
 is the word parakaleo.

915
00:36:41,220 --> 00:36:44,460
 And the idea is to urge someone towards something.

916
00:36:44,460 --> 00:36:45,700
 It's what I did at the beginning of this.

917
00:36:45,700 --> 00:36:46,920
 I didn't even realize I was doing that.

918
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:48,620
 But as I'm urging you to come with me,

919
00:36:48,620 --> 00:36:50,360
 I am appealing to you.

920
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:53,720
 I am parakaleoing you to jump in

921
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:55,680
 with what God has wanted to do at Awaken.

922
00:36:55,680 --> 00:36:57,100
 You've done this yourself.

923
00:36:57,100 --> 00:36:59,180
 Anybody ever try to get a baby to smile?

924
00:36:59,180 --> 00:37:01,540
 Yeah, that takes some serious effort.

925
00:37:01,540 --> 00:37:03,820
 Anybody try to work an angle to make a sale?

926
00:37:03,820 --> 00:37:04,680
 That takes some effort.

927
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:06,720
 Beg a friend to come out and be a part

928
00:37:06,720 --> 00:37:08,220
 of whatever that thing is that you don't wanna go to,

929
00:37:08,220 --> 00:37:09,360
 but you know you gotta go to?

930
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:10,960
 That takes some effort.

931
00:37:10,960 --> 00:37:12,840
 You're urging someone, appealing someone,

932
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:15,100
 persuading someone to come with you.

933
00:37:15,100 --> 00:37:17,400
 You are doing exactly what he is describing here.

934
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:19,880
 And what's crazy, track with me on this.

935
00:37:19,880 --> 00:37:20,880
 It's a little bit nerdy.

936
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:23,120
 But what's crazy about parakaleo

937
00:37:23,120 --> 00:37:25,080
 is that when you take it from its verb form

938
00:37:25,080 --> 00:37:26,700
 and you make it into a noun,

939
00:37:26,700 --> 00:37:28,720
 it turns into parakletos,

940
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:32,600
 which is another name for the Holy Spirit,

941
00:37:32,600 --> 00:37:35,760
 which means the one

942
00:37:35,760 --> 00:37:40,200
 that is calling you alongside

943
00:37:40,200 --> 00:37:43,720
 is the one

944
00:37:43,720 --> 00:37:49,260
 that has already been called alongside.

945
00:37:49,260 --> 00:37:50,120
 You see it?

946
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:53,120
 The Holy Spirit inside of you,

947
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:55,920
 the fire from heaven himself,

948
00:37:55,920 --> 00:38:00,640
 is the same one that is begging you to stay on the altar

949
00:38:00,640 --> 00:38:02,340
 so he can keep burning within you.

950
00:38:02,940 --> 00:38:05,580
 It is an immense kindness of God

951
00:38:05,580 --> 00:38:07,740
 that he is saying, "I am the fire,

952
00:38:07,740 --> 00:38:09,180
 "and I want you to stay close to me

953
00:38:09,180 --> 00:38:12,140
 "so I can continue to burn bright in your life."

954
00:38:12,140 --> 00:38:17,340
 But you gotta continue to give yourself willingly.

955
00:38:17,340 --> 00:38:25,500
 It's why, because the Spirit does this work so often,

956
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:27,300
 that feeling you have that you're supposed

957
00:38:27,300 --> 00:38:29,420
 to come down front or the prompting you get

958
00:38:29,420 --> 00:38:31,980
 to go and pray or the conviction you feel

959
00:38:31,980 --> 00:38:35,500
 to confess your sin or the urgency you get

960
00:38:35,500 --> 00:38:36,980
 to raise your hands in worship,

961
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:38,540
 even though you're fighting it so hard,

962
00:38:38,540 --> 00:38:40,300
 that is a prompting from the Spirit.

963
00:38:40,300 --> 00:38:41,820
 That is a work of the Spirit,

964
00:38:41,820 --> 00:38:43,580
 stirring in your life so that way

965
00:38:43,580 --> 00:38:45,540
 you would actually burn brighter

966
00:38:45,540 --> 00:38:49,160
 as he is inflamed further within your life.

967
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:50,380
 That's what's happening.

968
00:38:50,380 --> 00:38:52,260
 Why does he do this?

969
00:38:52,260 --> 00:38:55,780
 Why does God go to the trouble of appealing to you?

970
00:38:55,780 --> 00:38:58,260
 Literally, he could just coerce your obedience.

971
00:38:58,260 --> 00:39:00,780
 The guy spoke, and creation popped out.

972
00:39:00,780 --> 00:39:03,140
 It was just the most insane thing.

973
00:39:03,140 --> 00:39:07,100
 He does not need to have your compliance

974
00:39:07,100 --> 00:39:09,140
 in order to become a good Christian.

975
00:39:09,140 --> 00:39:10,340
 He could just make it so.

976
00:39:10,340 --> 00:39:12,580
 He could force you to do whatever he wanted,

977
00:39:12,580 --> 00:39:13,940
 and yet he doesn't do it.

978
00:39:13,940 --> 00:39:14,780
 Why?

979
00:39:14,780 --> 00:39:17,220
 Because there's no surrender without choice.

980
00:39:17,220 --> 00:39:18,940
 There's no surrender without choice.

981
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:21,540
 Like God, he could force obedience if he wanted to,

982
00:39:21,540 --> 00:39:24,300
 but he doesn't want your obligation.

983
00:39:24,300 --> 00:39:25,780
 He doesn't want your compliance.

984
00:39:25,780 --> 00:39:27,100
 He wants you to choose him.

985
00:39:27,100 --> 00:39:28,300
 He wants you to want him.

986
00:39:28,300 --> 00:39:30,460
 He wants you to desire him above anything

987
00:39:30,460 --> 00:39:32,900
 and everything else, because here's the thing.

988
00:39:32,900 --> 00:39:35,580
 Paul says that we should respond with spiritual worship.

989
00:39:35,580 --> 00:39:38,980
 There is no spiritual worship without desire.

990
00:39:38,980 --> 00:39:41,060
 Like you cannot sing the praises

991
00:39:41,060 --> 00:39:43,940
 of something you do not enjoy.

992
00:39:43,940 --> 00:39:44,760
 If you don't believe me,

993
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:47,140
 just look at any dad at the mall.

994
00:39:47,140 --> 00:39:49,940
 Every dad at the mall is so unhappy to be there.

995
00:39:49,940 --> 00:39:50,780
 Why?

996
00:39:50,780 --> 00:39:52,940
 Because they're not there shopping for themselves.

997
00:39:52,940 --> 00:39:55,920
 They're there buying for everyone else.

998
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:57,260
 They're so discontent.

999
00:39:57,260 --> 00:39:59,140
 They cannot sing the praise of the experience

1000
00:39:59,140 --> 00:40:01,300
 'cause they do not want to be there.

1001
00:40:01,300 --> 00:40:02,780
 I know there's some exceptions to this,

1002
00:40:02,780 --> 00:40:04,940
 but by and large, you don't see women

1003
00:40:04,940 --> 00:40:07,420
 normally geeking out about smoking meat.

1004
00:40:07,420 --> 00:40:10,100
 They don't just like show up to Home Depot

1005
00:40:10,100 --> 00:40:13,060
 and buy a power tool because might need it just in case.

1006
00:40:13,060 --> 00:40:16,140
 Like they're not admonishing the value of their VA.

1007
00:40:16,140 --> 00:40:17,500
 I'm not talking about vegetable juice.

1008
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:19,580
 Like normally what you see is you see

1009
00:40:19,580 --> 00:40:22,300
 that we have a tendency to praise the things

1010
00:40:22,300 --> 00:40:24,740
 that we actually legitimately enjoy.

1011
00:40:24,740 --> 00:40:26,460
 I can't believe I'm actually gonna admit this.

1012
00:40:26,460 --> 00:40:29,620
 I went and I saw Barbie in theaters.

1013
00:40:29,620 --> 00:40:32,300
 And the reason I did was not by way of my own choice.

1014
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:33,900
 I didn't wanna go.

1015
00:40:33,900 --> 00:40:36,980
 No part of me wants to be in that theater

1016
00:40:36,980 --> 00:40:39,460
 watching this and wearing pink.

1017
00:40:39,460 --> 00:40:40,860
 And yet I'm in that theater

1018
00:40:40,860 --> 00:40:42,580
 because a group of friends wanted us to be,

1019
00:40:42,580 --> 00:40:45,540
 and I was legitimately coerced into going.

1020
00:40:45,540 --> 00:40:47,500
 It was not by way of my decision.

1021
00:40:47,500 --> 00:40:50,460
 I was not there because I desired to be so.

1022
00:40:50,460 --> 00:40:51,500
 I am saying that to you

1023
00:40:51,500 --> 00:40:53,100
 because I need you to hear me on this.

1024
00:40:53,100 --> 00:40:54,420
 So many Christians,

1025
00:40:54,420 --> 00:40:58,300
 they have confused their worship with God

1026
00:40:58,300 --> 00:41:00,540
 in the same way that I,

1027
00:41:00,540 --> 00:41:03,120
 let me clarify what I wanna say.

1028
00:41:03,120 --> 00:41:05,700
 So many Christians today are trying to worship God

1029
00:41:05,700 --> 00:41:07,200
 the way that I watched Barbie.

1030
00:41:07,200 --> 00:41:10,060
 They don't wanna be in it.

1031
00:41:10,060 --> 00:41:12,180
 They feel totally obligated.

1032
00:41:12,180 --> 00:41:14,620
 They're having to comply because it's part of the job.

1033
00:41:14,620 --> 00:41:16,740
 They're being obedient because that is what's necessary.

1034
00:41:16,740 --> 00:41:18,380
 And yet God does not want that from us.

1035
00:41:18,380 --> 00:41:20,140
 Psalm 63, five through six says,

1036
00:41:20,140 --> 00:41:23,540
 "My soul will be satisfied as with fat and rich food.

1037
00:41:23,540 --> 00:41:25,820
 "My mouth will praise you with joyful lips

1038
00:41:25,820 --> 00:41:27,180
 "when I remember you upon my bed

1039
00:41:27,180 --> 00:41:29,220
 "and meditate on you in the watches of the night."

1040
00:41:29,220 --> 00:41:31,380
 That's not someone who is begrudgingly logging

1041
00:41:31,380 --> 00:41:32,620
 their next quiet time.

1042
00:41:32,620 --> 00:41:34,260
 That's someone who can't get any sleep

1043
00:41:34,260 --> 00:41:37,060
 'cause they can't stop thinking about God.

1044
00:41:37,060 --> 00:41:39,180
 That's what it looks like to desire him.

1045
00:41:39,180 --> 00:41:40,860
 They are just doing their Christianity.

1046
00:41:40,860 --> 00:41:43,340
 They legitimately desire Christ.

1047
00:41:43,340 --> 00:41:47,700
 John Wesley said, "Light yourself on fire with passion

1048
00:41:47,700 --> 00:41:51,020
 "and people will come from miles to watch you burn."

1049
00:41:52,620 --> 00:41:54,580
 Light yourself on fire.

1050
00:41:54,580 --> 00:41:56,620
 That is a totally voluntary decision.

1051
00:41:56,620 --> 00:41:59,580
 No one is offering themselves up for that to happen.

1052
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:02,460
 Everyone willingly says, "I will light myself on fire

1053
00:42:02,460 --> 00:42:04,660
 "for the very purposes of gathering people

1054
00:42:04,660 --> 00:42:07,300
 "to see what God is doing in my life."

1055
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:10,100
 In the Bible, burnt offerings, this is what's fascinating.

1056
00:42:10,100 --> 00:42:11,440
 They were not just whole offerings.

1057
00:42:11,440 --> 00:42:12,820
 They were not just daily offerings.

1058
00:42:12,820 --> 00:42:15,340
 They were the only voluntary offering,

1059
00:42:15,340 --> 00:42:20,100
 which meant they had to be given willingly.

1060
00:42:20,100 --> 00:42:21,700
 Are you willing in the same way?

1061
00:42:22,620 --> 00:42:27,220
 To go when no one else has, to move when no one else will,

1062
00:42:27,220 --> 00:42:30,020
 to stand when no one else does.

1063
00:42:30,020 --> 00:42:31,020
 And here's the thing.

1064
00:42:31,020 --> 00:42:33,860
 I know as I say all of that,

1065
00:42:33,860 --> 00:42:36,420
 some of you are unsure of what God is asking,

1066
00:42:36,420 --> 00:42:38,220
 to confess that sin, to forgive that friend,

1067
00:42:38,220 --> 00:42:39,340
 to take the risk, to seek some help,

1068
00:42:39,340 --> 00:42:41,100
 to approach that person, but here's what I would tell you,

1069
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:42,960
 and this is so important, I need you to listen.

1070
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:45,980
 You do not have to want what God is asking of you,

1071
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:48,380
 but you can trust the one who is asking of you.

1072
00:42:48,380 --> 00:42:50,420
 You don't have to want it.

1073
00:42:50,420 --> 00:42:52,600
 You don't have to want whatever he's asking you to do,

1074
00:42:52,600 --> 00:42:56,320
 but you can trust the fact that he is the one asking you.

1075
00:42:56,320 --> 00:42:57,160
 How do I know that?

1076
00:42:57,160 --> 00:42:59,820
 Because I know Jesus was in the exact same place.

1077
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:02,740
 We see it in the garden.

1078
00:43:02,740 --> 00:43:04,100
 Like Jesus in a position where

1079
00:43:04,100 --> 00:43:06,980
 he doesn't want to go to the cross.

1080
00:43:06,980 --> 00:43:09,660
 He doesn't want to suffer that indignity.

1081
00:43:09,660 --> 00:43:11,180
 You know he even asks God,

1082
00:43:11,180 --> 00:43:14,100
 "Hey, if we can find another way, I'm up for that."

1083
00:43:14,100 --> 00:43:16,980
 And yet, though he was unwanting to go,

1084
00:43:16,980 --> 00:43:19,520
 he was never unwilling to go.

1085
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:23,360
 He was willing to voluntarily offer himself.

1086
00:43:23,360 --> 00:43:25,640
 He says this himself in John 10.

1087
00:43:25,640 --> 00:43:28,760
 He says, "For this reason the Father loves me,

1088
00:43:28,760 --> 00:43:29,960
 "because I lay down my life,

1089
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:31,480
 "that I might take it up again.

1090
00:43:31,480 --> 00:43:34,020
 "No one takes it from me,

1091
00:43:34,020 --> 00:43:35,820
 "but I lay it down of my own accord."

1092
00:43:35,820 --> 00:43:40,240
 You see, Christ voluntarily gave his life for us,

1093
00:43:40,240 --> 00:43:43,780
 so we voluntarily give our life for him too.

1094
00:43:43,780 --> 00:43:48,880
 God is not interested in a sacrifice

1095
00:43:48,880 --> 00:43:51,960
 that comes to the altar kicking and screaming

1096
00:43:51,960 --> 00:43:53,760
 because it doesn't want to be there.

1097
00:43:53,760 --> 00:43:57,000
 God is interested in sacrifices

1098
00:43:57,000 --> 00:44:00,480
 that say, "Jesus, whatever you ask,

1099
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:04,220
 "wherever you lead, whatever you want, you have me."

1100
00:44:04,220 --> 00:44:06,080
 Does he have you?

1101
00:44:06,080 --> 00:44:16,120
 I'll close with this.

1102
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:17,820
 You know, it was one thing for me.

1103
00:44:18,820 --> 00:44:23,060
 To realize that I not only wanted to date Brooke,

1104
00:44:23,060 --> 00:44:24,560
 that I wanted to marry Brooke.

1105
00:44:24,560 --> 00:44:27,860
 And at the cost of doing so would mean

1106
00:44:27,860 --> 00:44:31,580
 all of me for all of her.

1107
00:44:31,580 --> 00:44:34,060
 And yet it was a different thing entirely

1108
00:44:34,060 --> 00:44:37,340
 for me to actually take this step, to make the decision.

1109
00:44:37,340 --> 00:44:43,080
 And yet, I remember it.

1110
00:44:43,080 --> 00:44:47,580
 Standing next to her on our wedding day

1111
00:44:47,580 --> 00:44:50,660
 before our closest family and friends

1112
00:44:50,660 --> 00:44:52,180
 on a cool October evening.

1113
00:44:52,180 --> 00:44:59,500
 Making the decision to willingly surrender all of myself,

1114
00:44:59,500 --> 00:45:02,060
 the entirety of who I was,

1115
00:45:02,060 --> 00:45:07,060
 every day of my life consistently for her sake,

1116
00:45:07,060 --> 00:45:10,720
 by way of my own choice, willingly.

1117
00:45:10,720 --> 00:45:17,540
 In an altar, wouldn't you know?

1118
00:45:18,540 --> 00:45:21,180
 (gentle music)

1119
00:45:21,180 --> 00:45:26,180
 And as I did so there, it was out of the recognition then

1120
00:45:26,180 --> 00:45:32,820
 in the increasing realization every day since

1121
00:45:32,820 --> 00:45:35,260
 that she was worth it.

1122
00:45:35,260 --> 00:45:37,100
 She was worth it.

1123
00:45:37,100 --> 00:45:41,620
 Friends, Jesus is worth it.

1124
00:45:41,620 --> 00:45:47,220
 Jesus is worth surrendering everything for.

1125
00:45:47,220 --> 00:45:48,060
 Why?

1126
00:45:48,060 --> 00:45:50,200
 Because he surrendered everything for you.

1127
00:45:50,200 --> 00:45:55,220
 Jesus offered himself entirely

1128
00:45:55,220 --> 00:45:58,420
 for all people that would place their faith in him.

1129
00:45:58,420 --> 00:46:00,380
 He offered the whole of who he was.

1130
00:46:00,380 --> 00:46:03,020
 He did not hold back any part of himself.

1131
00:46:03,020 --> 00:46:04,780
 No, he came from heaven to earth

1132
00:46:04,780 --> 00:46:07,980
 and he offered everything he had,

1133
00:46:07,980 --> 00:46:11,100
 the totality of the son of God,

1134
00:46:11,100 --> 00:46:15,860
 given for the totality of a sinful people, he did it.

1135
00:46:15,860 --> 00:46:18,620
 But he didn't just offer himself entirely.

1136
00:46:18,620 --> 00:46:23,620
 He offered himself consistently, every day, day by day,

1137
00:46:23,620 --> 00:46:26,700
 one choice after the next, the next step until the next.

1138
00:46:26,700 --> 00:46:29,460
 He kept going with this conviction

1139
00:46:29,460 --> 00:46:35,140
 that they're worth whatever the price.

1140
00:46:35,140 --> 00:46:40,800
 And he chose to offer himself willingly.

1141
00:46:42,020 --> 00:46:47,020
 No one, no one, but he would do what he did.

1142
00:46:47,020 --> 00:46:53,660
 And no one, no one could do what he and he alone did.

1143
00:46:53,660 --> 00:46:57,820
 He voluntarily put himself upon the cross,

1144
00:46:57,820 --> 00:47:01,860
 offered himself willingly for your sake.

1145
00:47:01,860 --> 00:47:04,020
 Not because there's anything in you or in me

1146
00:47:04,020 --> 00:47:05,780
 that would bait him to do so,

1147
00:47:05,780 --> 00:47:08,940
 but merely because he chose to lavish upon us his love,

1148
00:47:08,940 --> 00:47:12,340
 because he wanted us to be returned to right relationship.

1149
00:47:12,340 --> 00:47:15,460
 So that way God, who wishes to dwell amongst his people,

1150
00:47:15,460 --> 00:47:18,060
 may in fact be able to dwell amongst his people.

1151
00:47:18,060 --> 00:47:20,780
 And so in fact, he might dwell amongst us here.

1152
00:47:20,780 --> 00:47:25,740
 Everything we experienced this weekend,

1153
00:47:25,740 --> 00:47:30,120
 it is the by-product of Christ surrendering himself.

1154
00:47:30,120 --> 00:47:36,180
 And hear me, look, everything you experienced this weekend,

1155
00:47:38,540 --> 00:47:41,260
 one by one, individual by individual,

1156
00:47:41,260 --> 00:47:43,860
 everything you experienced here this weekend

1157
00:47:43,860 --> 00:47:47,860
 will be the result of you surrendering yourself in kind.

1158
00:47:47,860 --> 00:47:55,580
 Jesus put himself on the altar for your sake.

1159
00:47:55,580 --> 00:48:03,400
 Will you put yourself on the altar for his?

1160
00:48:03,400 --> 00:48:06,300
 Let me pray that you would.

1161
00:48:08,420 --> 00:48:10,140
 God, we're moving into a time now

1162
00:48:10,140 --> 00:48:13,500
 where we are about to do business with you,

1163
00:48:13,500 --> 00:48:15,660
 because God, this is what I know is true of this room.

1164
00:48:15,660 --> 00:48:17,340
 I'm grateful that it is true of this room.

1165
00:48:17,340 --> 00:48:20,740
 These are the hungriest of young adults in this room.

1166
00:48:20,740 --> 00:48:22,260
 People, God, that say,

1167
00:48:22,260 --> 00:48:26,100
 "I don't want a minor meager sort of Christian life.

1168
00:48:26,100 --> 00:48:29,340
 "I want all the way in, all the way up,

1169
00:48:29,340 --> 00:48:31,940
 "all I have to give kind of faith in God,

1170
00:48:31,940 --> 00:48:35,480
 "and I will do whatever it takes to get as much of Christ

1171
00:48:35,480 --> 00:48:37,420
 "and all that Christ has come to give."

1172
00:48:38,420 --> 00:48:39,540
 (gentle music)

1173
00:48:39,540 --> 00:48:43,060
 You say, God, that the sacrifices of God

1174
00:48:43,060 --> 00:48:46,940
 are a broken spirit, a broken and a contrite heart.

1175
00:48:46,940 --> 00:48:49,240
 Oh God, you will not despise that.

1176
00:48:49,240 --> 00:48:55,780
 That is the proper sacrifice unto you.

1177
00:48:55,780 --> 00:48:57,640
 So God, would we do that now?

1178
00:48:57,640 --> 00:49:01,460
 Would we do that now, God?

1179
00:49:01,460 --> 00:49:05,220
 Not because we're performative Christians,

1180
00:49:05,220 --> 00:49:08,540
 not because there's a pressure around

1181
00:49:08,540 --> 00:49:11,100
 to respond the way everyone else is.

1182
00:49:11,100 --> 00:49:12,500
 That would be conforming to the world,

1183
00:49:12,500 --> 00:49:13,980
 and you've told us not to conform to the world,

1184
00:49:13,980 --> 00:49:16,260
 but God, do you want to transform us from the inside out?

1185
00:49:16,260 --> 00:49:17,260
 And so God, in this moment,

1186
00:49:17,260 --> 00:49:21,200
 would we do everything we've discussed

1187
00:49:21,200 --> 00:49:22,800
 with brokenness and contrition?

1188
00:49:22,800 --> 00:49:26,700
 Would we come before you, God, back to the altar,

1189
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:29,700
 bringing whatever it is, God, we need to give?

1190
00:49:29,700 --> 00:49:31,820
 If we've withheld something from you, God,

1191
00:49:31,820 --> 00:49:33,180
 if we've not given the entirety of ourselves,

1192
00:49:33,180 --> 00:49:36,100
 would we come and would we give it all tonight?

1193
00:49:36,100 --> 00:49:37,500
 Think about that for you.

1194
00:49:37,500 --> 00:49:41,340
 Is there anything in your life that you know,

1195
00:49:41,340 --> 00:49:43,820
 God has had his finger on that for a long time,

1196
00:49:43,820 --> 00:49:46,320
 and I just have not wanted to give it over to him?

1197
00:49:46,320 --> 00:49:51,140
 But tonight, you can have it, God.

1198
00:49:51,140 --> 00:49:53,580
 You can have it, God, because you can have me.

1199
00:49:53,580 --> 00:50:00,220
 Would you work, God, to reveal if there's any area

1200
00:50:00,220 --> 00:50:02,460
 where we're not consistently giving of ourselves?

1201
00:50:02,460 --> 00:50:05,300
 If we've quenched your fire,

1202
00:50:05,300 --> 00:50:09,000
 if God, we have indulged willful sin,

1203
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:11,200
 if there is unconfessed sin,

1204
00:50:11,200 --> 00:50:14,740
 if God, we have done anything to douse

1205
00:50:14,740 --> 00:50:15,940
 the flame of your indwelling,

1206
00:50:15,940 --> 00:50:18,500
 would we, God, do everything we can

1207
00:50:18,500 --> 00:50:19,940
 to move as far away from it

1208
00:50:19,940 --> 00:50:21,940
 as we move as close to you as we can?

1209
00:50:21,940 --> 00:50:27,700
 And then God, we're going to be tested now

1210
00:50:27,700 --> 00:50:30,380
 if we will willingly offer ourselves.

1211
00:50:30,380 --> 00:50:32,960
 (gentle music)

1212
00:50:32,960 --> 00:50:37,000
 If we will volunteer ourselves into the awkward,

1213
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:40,940
 volunteer ourselves into the uncomfortable,

1214
00:50:40,940 --> 00:50:45,120
 volunteer ourselves into that which costs.

1215
00:50:45,120 --> 00:50:50,460
 But it's worth doing 'cause we trust you.

1216
00:50:50,460 --> 00:50:53,040
 Lord, we need you now.

1217
00:50:53,040 --> 00:50:55,360
 Minister to us.

1218
00:50:59,660 --> 00:51:01,860
 A life on the altar, oh Christ.

1219
00:51:01,860 --> 00:51:03,400
 That's what we come to give.

1220
00:51:03,400 --> 00:51:05,580
 A life on fire, oh Christ.

1221
00:51:05,580 --> 00:51:07,220
 That's what we come to give.

1222
00:51:07,220 --> 00:51:08,700
 Fan the flame.

1223
00:51:08,700 --> 00:51:10,020
 Have us all.

1224
00:51:10,020 --> 00:51:12,940
 Meet us here in your name, amen.

1225
00:51:12,940 --> 00:51:15,320
 Space is open.

1226
00:51:15,320 --> 00:51:18,060
 Altar is free.

1227
00:51:18,060 --> 00:51:22,280
 These team members to my right and to my left,

1228
00:51:22,280 --> 00:51:24,580
 they'd love to pray with you.

1229
00:51:24,580 --> 00:51:28,460
 And the good news is you know there's no need to rush out

1230
00:51:29,580 --> 00:51:31,140
 because you're here all weekend.

1231
00:51:31,140 --> 00:51:34,980
 But why wait another moment

1232
00:51:34,980 --> 00:51:37,180
 when Christ didn't wait a moment to come for you?

1233
00:51:37,180 --> 00:51:40,020
 Come to him and let him have yourself, please.

